1235:{"seq":1235,"at":"2026-09-10T21:04:17.623Z","actor":"agent","type":"note.added","payload":{"node":"werk-mc-askqa","text":"Deny already carries a free-text 'message' back to the model as the tool result (agent.ts:687). The likely path: keep this an ordinary deny, but set message to the chosen option's label instead of the fixed denial line. Client-side, parse a.input.questions[].options[] and render real buttons instead of dumping a.label. Unverified: whether the model then reads that message as a normal answer, or whether AskUserQuestion needs a distinct response subtype the control protocol doesn't expose yet. Needs a build to check, not a talk-through."}}
1246:{"seq":1246,"at":"2026-09-10T21:13:59.240Z","actor":"agent","type":"note.added","payload":{"node":"werk-mc-askqa","text":"Built and verified live: web/app.js renders a.input.questions as question text + option buttons (single-select replaces the pick, multiSelect toggles), a 'Submit answer' button composes 'For \"<question>\": <picked label(s)>' per question. It goes back over the existing deny channel — permission.ts's Asks.answer/put now carry an optional message alongside the decision, and agent.ts's deny response uses it in place of the fixed denial line. Confirmed end to end after a real server restart (the serve() HMR guard from #werk-hmr does not cover this code): the model received the composed answer text as the tool result, not a denial."}}
